> Ever find a snake or spider obviously move under say a food ration
> and become invisible (on the screen)?  Then you move to attack and
> the game specifically acts as though you just discovered the monster.

Wait-- there's a cave spider hiding under that cave spider corpse!


As far as command changes go, keep Shift-direction doing what it is.  No, it
ain't perfect, but it doesn't attack anything, and I use it a lot.  I rather
like the idea of F toggling in and out of fight-mode, perhaps with the
default settable from NETHACKOPTIONS.  I *certainly* dread the concept of
having to hit "f" every turn I want to attack a monster, and this might even
be enough to get me to stop playing the game (as, I suspect, is the case with
many others; do *you* want to use twice as many keystrokes as you should have
to?)

As far as pools/&c go, I agree that you shouldn't die just by walking into
them; come on, you certainly have more common sense than to do that, and
besides, it's as frustrating as hell.  You *should* die by falling in if
you are confused, and I also agree that running into walls should require
a turn when confused.  Same if you're blind or hallucinating.  (In fact, I
find it quite amazing how well one can search when blind.)

Just my opinions-- sorry I haven't said anything new.

